# The llama.cpp pins, one b-build per host class, and the repository of ggml's images. A class's
# build serves each of its flavors: host/llama.sh names the server image server-<flavor>-<build> in
# LLAMA_REPOSITORY, and llama_pin (host/llama-release.sh) reads the class's pin. LLAMA_RELEASE is
# the semver release last pinned, v0.8.0, whose notes ("Nightly build:") name b11960; neither class
# runs it now. gb10 (gb10-1; cuda13) and strix-halo (the Framework; rocm and vulkan) run b12464,
# the newest build with every flavor's server image on ghcr.io (server-cuda13-, server-rocm- and
# server-vulkan-b12464) on 2026-11-17, which spike-model-gateway's priority task moved both classes
# to (the architect's review escalation, docs/findings/priority.md there). That ended the hold on
# b12098: llama.cpp #31620 and #31639 (b12100 and later) match an -hf quantization tag only after
# `-`, `.` or `/`, and Google's 26B-A4B, 31B and E4B QAT GGUFs (such as gemma-4-26B_q4_0-it.gguf)
# put `_` before it, so their sections may not resolve on b12464. llama.cpp is inert on both hosts,
# which serve vLLM's rows, and b12464 is unverified: no section has started or served on it. The
# Framework's re-screen of Gemma 4 26B-A4B waits on llama.cpp #25584, the fix for #29221 (Vulkan's
# "tensor not allocated" abort on a 15-slot section's second request), and #31418 (Vulkan's
# batched tensor copy API) (spike-hosting-upgrades, docs/screens/framework/2026-11-04.md and
# docs/screens/gb10-1/2026-11-05.md). scripts/currency.sh compares each class's pin with the
# newest b-build that has the class's server image on ghcr.io, not with LLAMA_RELEASE's build.
# Sourced by host/llama-release.sh.
LLAMA_RELEASE=v0.8.0
LLAMA_BUILD_GB10=b12464
LLAMA_BUILD_STRIX_HALO=b12464
LLAMA_REPOSITORY=ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp
